Id: sudo001w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_sudo
Fix: Remove NOPASSWD with visudo, or limit it to the commands that run unattended.
References: sudoers(5)
Controls: CIS 5.4; NIST AC-6; ISO 8.2; CE User access control

The named user or group (%group) may run any command as root through
sudo without typing a password (NOPASSWD: ALL). The password prompt is
what stands between a stolen session, a malicious script run by that
user, or someone at an unlocked screen, and root: without it, any code
running as that user is root whenever it likes. Cloud images often set
this for their default user.

To fix it, remove the NOPASSWD: tag from the rule (in /etc/sudoers or
the file under /etc/sudoers.d that holds it, with visudo), or limit
NOPASSWD to the specific commands that must run unattended. If the
account is used only with a key and nothing else runs as it, accept the
finding with tigris-accept.
